{:id :EACL-FORMAL-035
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :benchmark
 :seed-or-trace
 "authority-mode/datascript/recursive-and-cursor/64-groups/64-documents"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :performance
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 commit 2c3065e2468c199ad9a2947766471936bd8e42c2"]
 :affected-backends [:datascript :datahike :datomic]
 :root-cause
 "The handwritten CLJ-to-generated-Java indexed conversion boundary invoked generated variant, destructor, and BigInteger methods without concrete type hints. Clojure therefore performed reflective method lookup on every generated drive/resume/scan round trip. The semantic model and opaque state were correct, but the trusted FFI boundary added avoidable allocation and latency."
 :fix
 "The Java conversion boundary now statically dispatches every generated variant, result, state, projection, command, counter, and numeric conversion call. A compile-time reflection audit covers the complete boundary source, while the generated-only heavy and resource gates separately measure latency, caller-thread allocation, backend operations, and retained live heap."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.characterization-fixture-test/generated-java-boundary-is-reflection-free-test"
  "eacl.formal.verified-authority-suite/run-heavy!"
  "eacl.formal.retained-heap-benchmark/run!"
  "formal mutation :generated-java-boundary-restores-reflection"]}
